157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (The study does not represent the views of Digital Africa or Expertise France, and the views expressed also do not include those of Cage Patrick & Company Advocates, as its involvement was limited to the design, conduct, and analysis of this data landscape survey. The findings and recommendations in this report are those of the study team, grounded in primary data collected from 39 survey respondents and 12 qualitative interviews across the eight priority countries.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (The legal and regulatory dimensions of data use remain a significant barrier for many African startups particularly in sectors like agritech and food systems, where qualitative data are not easily available and sensitive commercial and environmental data are frequently involved. These barriers are compounded by a lack of adapted legal instruments, regulatory ambiguity, and limited access to legal expertise. This study sets out to document those barriers through the experiences of the startups themselves, and to translate those experiences into concrete, actionable recommendations.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
