/P 120 0 R
/E (The findings presented in this report are exploratory and qualitative in character. They reflect the experiences of a specific cohort of early-to-mid-stage African startups and should not be treated as statistically representative of the African tech ecosystem as a whole. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E (The study is designed to establish a baseline and generate actionable insights, with the expectation that annual repetition will build comparability over time. Potential sources of bias include self-reporting bias \(mitigated by anonymity and the toolkit incentive\), selection bias toward more digitally engaged startups \(mitigated by broad multi-channel outreach\), and recall bias in interview responses \(mitigated by focusing on recent, specific experiences\).)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
