214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 914 0 R
/T (AI adoption is active and accelerating but infrastructure, talent, and costs constrain scale. 47% of respondents are already running AI in production. The leading AI adoption barriers are the cost of AI tools, cloud services, and hardware, followed by data privacy concerns and concerns about the reliability of AI outputs. Unlike more general-purpose tech cohorts, regulatory uncertainty ranks lower than infrastructure and talent as an AI barrier in this sector-specific cohort.)
/E (AI adoption is active and accelerating but infrastructure, talent, and costs constrain scale. 47% of respondents are already running AI in production. The leading AI adoption barriers are the cost of AI tools, cloud services, and hardware, followed by data privacy concerns and concerns about the reliability of AI outputs. Unlike more general-purpose tech cohorts, regulatory uncertainty ranks lower than infrastructure and talent as an AI barrier in this sector-specific cohort.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 915 0 R
/T <>
/E <>
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 916 0 R
/T (Data sharing is widespread but inadequately governed. 69% of respondents have shared data with another organisation. Among those who have, the most common challenges are data security concerns, lack of formal agreements, unclear data ownership, and different data protection standards. Informal agreements \(meeting notes, email, verbal arrangements\) are common, creating governance gaps that undermine the trust needed for sustained collaboration.)
/E (Data sharing is widespread but inadequately governed. 69% of respondents have shared data with another organisation. Among those who have, the most common challenges are data security concerns, lack of formal agreements, unclear data ownership, and different data protection standards. Informal agreements \(meeting notes, email, verbal arrangements\) are common, creating governance gaps that undermine the trust needed for sustained collaboration.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 917 0 R
/T (The single most demanded support is better data-sharing platforms, followed by clearer laws and AI capacity building. Better data-sharing platforms \(42%\), clearer laws and regulations \(39%\), and technical training and AI capacity building \(39%\) are the top three support needs. Simplified legal templates and access to quality training data also feature prominently.)
/E (The single most demanded support is better data-sharing platforms, followed by clearer laws and AI capacity building. Better data-sharing platforms \(42%\), clearer laws and regulations \(39%\), and technical training and AI capacity building \(39%\) are the top three support needs. Simplified legal templates and access to quality training data also feature prominently.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 121 0 R
/T (The most actionable gap identified by this study is the mismatch between the data-sharing activity that is already occurring and the governance infrastructure supporting it. Most startups are sharing data but without adequate legal frameworks, technical standards, or trust mechanisms. Addressing this gap through practical legal templates, regional data standards, and targeted capacity building is the clearest immediate priority for the AI4Startups platform.)
/E (The most actionable gap identified by this study is the mismatch between the data-sharing activity that is already occurring and the governance infrastructure supporting it. Most startups are sharing data but without adequate legal frameworks, technical standards, or trust mechanisms. Addressing this gap through practical legal templates, regional data standards, and targeted capacity building is the clearest immediate priority for the AI4Startups platform.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
