/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (This finding warrants careful interpretation. For startups in agri-food and clean energy sectors that are actively seeking partnerships with governments, utilities, and international buyers, data protection laws can function as legitimising frameworks providing structure that builds partner confidence and enables formal collaboration. The positive view of regulation may also reflect the fact that many respondents have not yet encountered the full compliance burden at scale.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 129 0 R
/T (4.2 The Most Difficult Regulatory Areas)
/E (4.2 The Most Difficult Regulatory Areas)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
349 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (Despite the broadly positive view of regulation, specific compliance areas are widely experienced as difficult. Data governance and internal policies and data protection and privacy compliance are the top two difficult areas, each cited by roughly half of respondents. Cross-border transfer rules and data ownership are also significant pain points.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
