/Title (AI adoption is active and accelerating but infrastructure, talent, and costs constrain scale. 47% of respondents are already running AI in production. The leading AI adoption barriers are the cost of AI tools, cloud services, and hardware, followed by data privacy concerns and concerns about the reliability of AI outputs. Unlike more general-purpose tech cohorts, regulatory uncertainty ranks lower than infrastructure and talent as an AI barrier in this sector-specific cohort.)
