/Title (Data sharing is widespread but inadequately governed. 69% of respondents have shared data with another organisation. Among those who have, the most common challenges are data security concerns, lack of formal agreements, unclear data ownership, and different data protection standards. Informal agreements \(meeting notes, email, verbal arrangements\) are common, creating governance gaps that undermine the trust needed for sustained collaboration.)
